# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `make sanitize-thread` (QA-09).
#
# tokio's I/O driver: a thread builds a `ScheduledIo` and registers its fd with epoll; the driver
# thread gets the pointer back from epoll_wait. The kernel gives that handoff its ordering, which
# TSan does not model, so it reports a race on the initial memcpy. Reproduced with the engine
# alone (UDP socket start-up, no test code involved); a false positive in tokio, not in openLab.
# Matches only stacks through tokio's scheduled_io module.
race:tokio::runtime::io::scheduled_io
